course: dictionary
lesson: 4594
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can name a thing and also describe an action. Herd is a noun when it names a group: «a herd of cows» is a large group of animals that live and move together. Herd is a verb when it names an action: to herd means to move animals or people together as a group.
explain: Look at the words around herd to find its job. If a word like a or of comes before it, herd is probably a noun. In «The dog herded the sheep into the pen», herd is a verb, because the dog is doing the moving.
explain: Herd can also mean ordinary people who all do the same thing. «Follow the herd» means copying everyone else without stopping to think for yourself. Context tells you this is about people, not animals.
fact: A herd is a large group of one kind of animal that lives and moves together, such as cows, deer, elephants or horses.
fact: To herd means to move animals or people together as a group.
fact: «Herd» is a noun in «a herd of cows» and a verb in «herd the sheep».
fact: Animals in a herd stay together for safety: «A foal must walk soon so it can keep up with the herd and run from danger.»
fact: «Follow the herd» means doing what everyone else does without thinking.
exercise: «A herd of cows» is grazing on the hill. What is a herd? | A single cow standing alone | *A large group of animals that live and move together | A type of farm tractor | A small wooden fence
exercise: «A foal must walk soon so it can keep up with the herd.» Find and copy one word that names a group of animals that move together. | danger | *herd | foal | walk
exercise: What does «follow the herd» mean? | *Copy everyone else without thinking for yourself | Run away from danger | Count the animals in a field | Lead a group of animals to water
test: In «The farmers herded the sheep into the pen», what does herded mean? | Fed them hay with a spoon | Counted them one by one | *Moved together as a group | Sheared their wool
test: In «Let's herd the children back inside», is herd a noun or a verb? | *Verb | Adverb | Adjective | Noun
exam: In «the matriarch remembers a waterhole the herd hasn't visited for years», what does herd mean? | A word for a grandmother | A family trip in a car | *A group of animals that live and move together | A dry, empty waterhole
